      "confidence": "Weak",
      "note": "False positive. params[:id] only selects a record (and does so from current_channel.items -- see invariant 3); it never becomes part of the path. The path comes from blob.key, a random token generated by ActiveStorage, not user input. The only thing a user controls is the filename, which plays no part in the on-disk path: the test 'a filename containing path separators cannot escape the storage root' in test/integration/download_test.rb uploads a file named ../../etc/passwd and asserts it still lands under the storage root. send_data is not an option here -- it would read the entire file, potentially several GB, into memory."
